    <title>Pure Molecular Beam of Water Dimer</title>
    <updated>2019-07-08T09:27:20Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.08716v3" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1904.08716v3" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Spatial separation of water dimer from water monomer and larger water-clusters through the electric deflector is presented. A beam of water dimer with $93~\%$ purity and a rotational temperature of $1.5~$K was obtained. Following strong-field ionization using a $35~$fs laser pulse with a wavelength centered around $800~$nm and a peak intensity of $10^{14}~\text{W}/\text{cm}^2$ we observed proton transfer and $46~\%$ of the ionized water dimer broke apart into a hydronium ion $\text{H}_3\text{O}^+$ and neutral OH.</summary>
